<title>THAILAND: Thailand allows 1997 rice imports of 240,506 T.</title>
<headline>Thailand allows 1997 rice imports of 240,506 T.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading world rice exporter Thailand on Friday decided to allow rice imports of 240,506.11 tonnes in 1997 under World Trade Organisation obligations, Commerce Minister Narongchai Akarasanee said.  </p>
<p>The quota will be divided into two deliveries -- 114,240.41 tonnes during May-August and 126,265.71 tonnes for September-December, he told reporters.</p>
<p>Thailand expects to export 5.0 million tonnes of rice this year.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (6620 652-0642</p>
</text>
